A||||27||Tigger||Met Al Gore tonight!!!||||4||
Z||000000||Tigger||11-06-2000||10:21 PM||||I met him just hours ago and had the chance to briefly talk to him and shake his hand.<P>Just last night I found out he was going to stop in my home town AGAIN, so I figured I should go and hear what he had to say.<P>From what I heard tonight, I see Gore's vision of continuing the prosperity we all have gained from the last 8 years.<P>I know for a fact he has done a lot to reduce the size of government... it was one of his objectives during the Clinton/Gore years.  He has did a lot to eliminate the $1000 toilet seats, etc. which has allowed our government to create a surplus, the first surplus in 40 years.<P>Al Gore isn't for HUGE government, he isn't going to take our guns away (they have been telling us that for years anyway, it will never happen), he isn't going to take away our internal combustion engines either.<P>The way I see it there are two alternatives in this election...  One, we can go back to the old trickle down economics of the Reagan and Bush years, promised tax cuts that never happened, and the creation of the largest deficits in government history.  Or two, we can continue to move forward, keeping 8 years of prosperity growing, keep the stock market up, and keep interest rates down.<P>I know many of you may argue that we are not better off than we were 8 years ago, or have other opinions and that's fair.<P>So, I encourage all of you who are registered to go out and vote on election day!<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue.gif"> ||||reg||4
