Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||11-06-2000||11:58 PM||||This is why I don't like to vote on major things like this. I don't understand the issues well enough, so instead of just voting for whoever has lied most convincingly... I choose not to vote, unless it's an issue that I understand 100%, or is just an opinion vote. (like when my town amalgamated with 4 others, and we had to vote on the name of the new minicipality.. one of the options was "Kinbruton".. LOL.. I chose to stick with the current name of Kincardine. so did most of the other people who voted.)<P>yes, it's my right to vote. but that doesn't mean I have to, and it also doesn't mean I don't have the right to complain about a government which I didn't participate in electing. An uninformed vote is useless IMHO, as it just indicates who was the best at lying and dissing their opponents. So, instead of being hypocritical.. I don't vote. btw, we're having elections soon in Canada as well.<P>&lt;rant mode off&gt;  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||4
