Z||000009||DaRkLoRD||11-07-2000||12:57 AM||||Unfortunately I don't follow politics *at all*, so I really can't comment on the gun laws here.. I personally don't own a gun, so I figure the laws don't directly apply to me anyway.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>a good friend of the family was in the canadian military for many years, and 2 years ago he applied to get a handgun to use at the local gun club/firing range.. it still took him over a year to get all the proper clearances etc, and he has very strict regulations about storing the gun, transporting it, etc. yeah, it can be a pain in the @ss I guess, but I'd prefer that to a situation where I'd worry about someone pulling a gun on me at school.. for the most part, that's simply not a big problem in canada...<P>anyway, sorry for getting so off-topic....<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
